{
  "name": "Encorp | Homework | Week 03 | HW 03 | Smart Content Categorizer",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Smart Content Categorizer (Week 03 / HW 03)\nWebhook -> validate -> **202 Accepted** -> Split Out -> Text Classifier -> Edit (category, timestamp) -> Merge -> single statistic (Aggregate) -> Data Table. Spam goes to the **Other** branch -> sub-workflow *Reject Article* (Stop and Error).\n\n**Coverage:** R1 Manual Trigger + Test Articles + Send Test Request + Webhook | R2 Split Out | R3 Text Classifier | R4 five Set nodes | R5 Other -> Send To Reject Article (Stop and Error inside) | R6 Merge + Select Title And Text + Aggregate Articles (+ Save To Data Table) | R7/R8 separate Error Handler workflow (Telegram).\n\n**Decisions**\n- The task does not say what the webhook returns and webhooks are fire-and-forget, so we answer immediately with **202 Accepted** (400 for an invalid body). Volume is unknown, so we must not wait for N LLM calls inside the HTTP timeout.\n- 202 and not 201: nothing is created yet, the request is only accepted.\n- Stop and Error fails the WHOLE execution, which would throw away the good articles. So it lives in a tiny sub-workflow, called once per spam article without waiting. Only that mini-execution fails; the Error workflow reports it (title + text are in the error message) and valid articles are processed anyway.\n- Five Set nodes: the classifier does not add the category to the item, only the branch knows it.\n- The statistic is one array of `{title, text}` built by Aggregate Articles (after Merge).\n- Data Table `smart_content_statistics` is the hand-over point: ONE row per run holding that statistic, so an external system (or a later scheduled workflow) can poll it. Columns: `batchId` (execution id), `generatedAt`, `articleCount`, `statistic` (the array as a JSON string, because data table columns are scalar). The reader parses it with JSON.parse. Nothing is returned to the caller.\n- If a run has no valid articles, nothing is written.\n- Do NOT enable Continue On Fail on Text Classifier: on error it emits the item on the first output (Technology).\n\n**Setup:** connect OpenRouter + Telegram credentials, create the Data Table `smart_content_statistics` (columns: batchId String, generatedAt String, articleCount Number, statistic String), set the Reject Article workflow in Send To Reject Article, put your n8n URL in Send Test Request, ACTIVATE the workflow (production webhook), set the Error Handler as Error workflow in the Settings of both workflows.",
        "height": 760,
        "width": 1000
      },
